<h2 id="watch">What to Watch For</h2>
<p>None of these four are guaranteed significant snaps once the regular season starts, but the Hall of Fame Game is where combine testing numbers get their first real football context. A fast 40 time means something different once there's a defender trying to stop you from using it. Kickoff is Thursday, August 6 at 8 p.m. ET from Tom Benson Hall of Fame Stadium in Canton, airing on NBC.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Do starters play in the Hall of Fame Game?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Rarely, or only for a series or two. The game is typically used to evaluate rookies and depth-chart battles rather than risk starters in the first preseason action of the year, especially for teams already deep into camp.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why does the Hall of Fame Game happen before other preseason games?</div>
<div class="faq-a">It's scheduled earlier than the rest of the preseason as part of the annual Hall of Fame enshrinement weekend in Canton, Ohio, giving the two selected teams an extra game and an earlier start to their preseason slate.</div>
</div>
